{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And what remains of it.</b> Scripture restored it, because above it said ״והנותרת מן המנחה לאהרן ולבניו.״ One might say: even all of what remains goes up to Heaven (i.e., is burned entirely). Scripture therefore says: ״והנותרת ממנה יאכלו אהרן ובניו״ — for the priests." "<b>Matzot shall be eaten.</b> Since it was included in the general permission (of food to priests), then forbidden, and then permitted again — one might think it returns to its original permissive status. Scripture therefore says: ״מצות תאכל״ — a commandment. Like its counterpart: ״יבמה יבא עליה״ — a commandment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:15.184293494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}